2. Changes!

These are the changes I've made in this version:

* RYLWEEN IS NOW ALSO A CLI DOOR! This means that it's not restricted
  to XENOLINK anymore! To run Rylween as a CLI door, use the
  following syntax: RYLWEEN <CLI> <Username>

  For Example:

  Rylween cli "Marcus Lagergren"
  Rylween cli TestUser

  It is still runnable as a XLK door though.
	If you for some strange reason want to run Rylween as a CLI door
  from _within_ Xenolink, use this command:

  CLIDOOR "Rylween CLI ~100"

  The CLI-Door does not check baud rate or ANSI compatibility. Find
  another way to restrict entry.
  The CLI-Door updates its graphics a bit slower than the Xeno door.

* You can no longer press the wrong key in combat and skip a character
  by mistake. Thanks to Mike Soucy for reporting this bug.

* There is a more prompt after the title screen.

* You can no longer talk to people who don't exist.
  Bug report by Per Wennerstrom.

* You can no longer walk around with four dead characters who
  have all starved to death. Bug report by Per Wennerstrom & Vicente
  Nicola.

* There is now a 50% chance of a mana point regenerating each turn.
  The previous 33% regenereated mana too slowly.

* Various other small changes.

Thanks go to these registered people:
--
Per Wennerstrom (First One), Micke Persson, David Hartje, Stephen Price.

